Planets on or near the Ascendant (typically within 10 degrees) act as a secondary "mask" and profoundly alter the expression of the rising sign
. These planets possess "accidental dignity," meaning their power and visibility in the individual's life are greatly magnified
.
Because the Ascendant is a calculated mathematical point rather than a physical body, it only receives aspects
. An aspect to the Ascendant colors the person's identity, physical appearance, and outward projection, but it does not alter the core expression of the aspecting planet itself
.



